---
sarib: 0.1
vocab: std@0.1
title: .sarib Decision Log
---

# Decision Log {#decision-log}

## D-001: Specify .sarib as a five-layer stack {.decision #d-001} ^d-001
date:: 2026-07-14
stage:: 1
status:: provisional
reversal:: Stage 2 produces evidence that layer separation caused prior-format failures (rather than preventing them).

(b). Lower layers freeze earlier; syntax is the last layer decided.

## D-002: Optimize tokens-per-interaction, not tokens-per-byte {.decision #d-002} ^d-002
date:: 2026-07-14
stage:: 1
status:: provisional
reversal:: Rule-6 benchmarks show syntax overhead dominates real agent workloads.

(b).

## D-003: Write loose, store canonical {.decision #d-003} ^d-003
date:: 2026-07-14
stage:: 1
status:: provisional
reversal:: The dialect/canonical split confuses users or fragments the ecosystem in practice.

(c). Humans write the dialect; tools normalize; agents edit via ops.

## D-004: History belongs to the substrate; diffability belongs to the format {.decision #d-004} ^d-004
date:: 2026-07-14
stage:: 1
status:: provisional
reversal:: Op-log interchange requirements (multi-agent sync) exceed what external substrates can carry.

(b).

## D-005: Identity, concurrency, provenance, adoption are first-class pillars {.decision #d-005} ^d-005
date:: 2026-07-14
stage:: 1
status:: provisional
reversal:: N/A (scope decision; individual pillars may be descoped with logged rationale).

Added to the requirement set; each gets dedicated research (RQ1, RQ6, RQ8) and model-level treatment (Stages 4–5, 8).

## D-006: Surface is a Markdown superset {.decision #d-006} ^d-006
date:: 2026-07-14
stage:: 2
status:: provisional
reversal:: Markdown-superset constraints prove to block a required model feature that no extension mechanism can carry.

A `.sarib` file must render acceptably as Markdown in a standard CommonMark renderer; the format is a Markdown superset, not a novel grammar. Incremental adoption one file/block at a time.

## D-007: Labeled property-graph model; reject RDF/triples lineage {.decision #d-007} ^d-007
date:: 2026-07-14
stage:: 2
status:: provisional
reversal:: A property-graph model proves unable to express a required knowledge pattern that triples handle natively.

(b) — nodes + typed edges carrying properties; native lists; no IRI ceremony.

## D-008: Closed-world validation; segregated inference; claims-not-truth {.decision #d-008} ^d-008
date:: 2026-07-14
stage:: 2
status:: provisional
reversal:: Single-author use shows provenance/claim overhead outweighs its value (would narrow, not remove).

Validate documents like a type system (closed-world, unique names). Keep derived/inferred facts visibly separate from asserted facts. Model stores attributable claims with provenance, not adjudicated truth.

## D-009: Round-trip law: identity + single-owner-per-state-class {.decision #d-009} ^d-009
date:: 2026-07-14
stage:: 2
status:: provisional
reversal:: None foreseen; this is the empirically strongest finding in the corpus.

Every atom gets a stable, position-independent, collision-proof ID that all projections carry. Projections are windows that may hide but never silently drop fields. Content / derived-cache / session state are separate layers, one writer each.

## D-010: Division of labor — humans write prose, agents enrich to graph {.decision #d-010} ^d-010
date:: 2026-07-14
stage:: 2
status:: provisional
reversal:: Evidence that target users will and do hand-author dense structure inline (would restore symmetric authoring).

"Human-writable" is satisfied by the surface being prose with *optional* light structure; the graph is mostly agent-produced and human-confirmed. LLMs make this viable now precisely because the structuring labor can move to the agent — though extraction cost/reliability (RQ7) must be respected by favoring incremental write-time structuring over bulk extraction.

## D-011: One in-core extension mechanism with graceful degradation {.decision #d-011} ^d-011
date:: 2026-07-14
stage:: 2
status:: provisional
reversal:: A generic extension slot proves to enable ambiguity that breaks deterministic parsing.

One blessed in-core attribute/extension mechanism. Unknown constructs must parse, render generically, and round-trip untouched. Core grammar frozen; extensions self-announcing and versioned separately.

## D-012: Edges emerge from prose; inline typed links are the primary edge mechanism {.decision #d-012} ^d-012
date:: 2026-07-15
stage:: 3
status:: provisional
reversal:: User testing shows inline link syntax disrupts prose more than block-form edge lists do.

(b). The primary edge-authoring act is an inline typed link within a natural sentence; block-form edge lists remain for cases prose can't carry but are not privileged.

## D-013: Containment is a zero-ceremony implicit edge; model distinguishes containment from cross-reference {.decision #d-013} ^d-013
date:: 2026-07-15
stage:: 3
status:: provisional
reversal:: The containment/cross-reference distinction proves to confuse authors or complicate the model without payoff.

Document hierarchy (headings, lists, nesting) compiles to zero-ceremony **containment edges**; the model distinguishes containment edges from **cross-reference edges**. ~~Containment is a DAG (multiple parents allowed), not a strict tree.~~ → **Amended by D-016 (Stage 4):** storage containment is a *single-parent, ordered spanning tree* (one home per node); multi-parent structure is delivered by transclusion (a cross-reference edge), not by multiple containment homes. The containment/cross-reference distinction itself stands.

## D-014: Operations name identified elements, never positions; op set designed for commutativity; retraction not deletion {.decision #d-014} ^d-014
date:: 2026-07-15
stage:: 3
status:: provisional
reversal:: Multi-agent concurrency requirements force a live CRDT store as canonical truth in v1 (file demotes to journal/snapshot — still specified).

Every edit operation references node/edge IDs (per D-009), never line/array positions. Prefer difference-form/commutative ops. Deletion is a status assertion (retraction), not erasure. v1 targets clean git 3-way merges on stable IDs + normal form; op vocabulary is CRDT-ready without model changes.

## D-015: One node type, progressively typed {.decision #d-015} ^d-015
date:: 2026-07-15
stage:: 4
status:: provisional
reversal:: Modeling entities and prose uniformly forces one to carry cost or ceremony that a split model would avoid.

A paragraph and an entity ("Alice") are the same object — a node = (id, optional type, content, properties, status, provenance). Prose is an untyped node with content; an entity is a typed node with properties. Proven at scale by Notion's "everything is a block."

## D-016: Storage containment is a single-parent spanning tree; multi-parent via transclusion (amends D-013) {.decision #d-016} ^d-016
date:: 2026-07-15
stage:: 4
status:: provisional
reversal:: A use case requires genuinely multiple equal homes that transclusion cannot model acceptably.

Storage containment is a rooted, ordered, single-parent **spanning tree** (each node has exactly one home). Multi-parent/appears-in-many-places structure is delivered by **transclusion** — a cross-reference edge (`transcludes`), not a second home. The document is the containment tree walked in order; edits through a transclusion flow to the one home (edit-consistent by construction).

## D-017: Edges are first-class, identified objects {.decision #d-017} ^d-017
date:: 2026-07-15
stage:: 4
status:: provisional
reversal:: First-class edge identity proves to cost more than the reification it avoids.

An edge = (id, type, family, source, target, order?, anchor?, properties, status, provenance). Edges have identity and properties like nodes — the labeled-property-graph advantage (D-007).

## D-018: Thin core; all semantic types are optional namespaced vocabulary {.decision #d-018} ^d-018
date:: 2026-07-15
stage:: 4
status:: provisional
reversal:: A semantic type proves so universal it must be core to keep the model coherent.

The core defines only one node, two edge families, a few structural roles (`document`/`section`/`prose`/`list`/`item`), and the extension mechanism. Every semantic type (`task`, `person`, `decision`, `api`, `motion`, …) is a schema in an optional standard library, namespaced. Unknown types parse, degrade, and round-trip untouched.

## D-019: Sparse, owner-defaulted provenance; assertion class + status enums {.decision #d-019} ^d-019
date:: 2026-07-15
stage:: 4
status:: provisional
reversal:: Sparse provenance proves ambiguous in multi-agent use, forcing explicit provenance everywhere.

Implicit provenance = "asserted by file owner," never materialized. Provenance materializes only when non-default (agent `inferred`, external `imported`, other author, stated basis). Assertion class ∈ {asserted, inferred, imported}; status ∈ {active, retracted}, retraction not erasure.

## D-020: Reclassify the brief's pseudo-types {.decision #d-020} ^d-020
date:: 2026-07-15
stage:: 5
status:: provisional
reversal:: A required fact pattern genuinely needs true hyperedges (>2 endpoints) that qualifiers can't model.

`dependency`/`relationship` → edge types; `constraint`/`risk`/`priority` → properties; n-ary and time-qualified facts → edges with qualifier properties (Wikidata model), so no hyperedges in v1.

## D-021: Core standard vocabulary v0 (eight kinds) + inclusion test {.decision #d-021} ^d-021
date:: 2026-07-15
stage:: 5
status:: provisional
reversal:: Dogfooding shows a kind unused or a "domain" type universal → revise via vocab versioning.

Core vocab v0 = {`task`, `decision`, `question`, `goal`, `event`, `agent`, `source`, `concept`}, admitted only if domain-agnostic AND behavior-changing AND irreducible. Domain sets (`sarib-software`, `sarib-design`) are separate optional vocabularies. All ship as optional schemas (per D-018).

## D-022: Transitive/inverse/symmetric relations are query-time, never materialized {.decision #d-022} ^d-022
date:: 2026-07-15
stage:: 5
status:: provisional
reversal:: Query-time derivation is too slow at scale and caching with provenance proves insufficient (RA5).

Declare algebraic properties (transitive/inverse/symmetric) as edge-type metadata; compute closures/inverses at query time (Stage 7). Any persisted derivation carries `inferred` provenance (D-019) and is regenerable.

## D-023: Schemas are self-hosted .sarib; validation closed-world + lint-grade {.decision #d-023} ^d-023
date:: 2026-07-15
stage:: 5
status:: provisional
reversal:: Self-hosting proves too weak to express needed constraints, forcing a dedicated schema language.

Schemas are `.sarib` documents (self-hosting), with a self-describing meta-schema. Validation is closed-world (unknown-vs-active-schema = diagnostic, no open-world inference) and lint-grade (non-fatal, P15).

## D-024: Deterministic reference resolution; ambiguity never guesses {.decision #d-024} ^d-024
date:: 2026-07-15
stage:: 5
status:: provisional
reversal:: Nearest-in-containment proves counter-intuitive in testing → revise the order (not the never-guess rule).

Resolution order — explicit id/slug → nearest-in-containment → document-global → vocabulary → unresolved. Multiple equally-near matches or none → unresolved (valid, renders as text, lint diagnostic). Never a silent guess. Matching after NFC + case-fold + whitespace-collapse; slugs exact. Pure function of (ref, document, active vocabs).

## D-025: Core never versions; vocabularies are semver, pinned, additive-only {.decision #d-025} ^d-025
date:: 2026-07-15
stage:: 5
status:: provisional
reversal:: Additive-only proves impossible for a needed correction that isn't a clean major bump.

Core constructs frozen at v1. Vocabularies semver-versioned, pinned per document; additive-only within a major (new kinds/optional props/edges); breaking changes → new namespace. Unknown vocab/version degrades gracefully (P17). Deprecate-not-delete (mirrors P12).

## D-026: Traversal is one parameterized walk; 13 traversals reduce to presets + strategies {.decision #d-026} ^d-026
date:: 2026-07-15
stage:: 6
status:: provisional
reversal:: A required traversal cannot be expressed as a setting of the seven axes.

Traversal is one primitive parameterized on seven axes — start · edge-selector · direction · frontier-order · filter · bound · derivation. 10 of the brief's 13 are presets; 3 (AI-selected, parallel, comparative) are composition strategies that drive the walk. Priority/chronological are the degenerate "no-edge" case (ordered selection of a set).

## D-027: Traversal is cycle-safe by construction; "acyclic" is a lint expectation {.decision #d-027} ^d-027
date:: 2026-07-15
stage:: 6
status:: provisional
reversal:: None foreseen; unconditional cycle-safety is required for robustness.

Every walk keeps a visited-set keyed by node id and emits each node once; this holds regardless of declared edge algebra. A real cycle yields a finite walk + a `cycle-detected` diagnostic. "Acyclic" is a validation expectation (lint), never a traversal precondition.

## D-028: Every traversal is bounded; results are subgraph + continuation cursor {.decision #d-028} ^d-028
date:: 2026-07-15
stage:: 6
status:: provisional
reversal:: A required use case cannot be served by bounded+cursor paging.

A traversal spec always carries a bound (max-depth / max-nodes / subgraph boundary); the standard interface has no unbounded traversal. Results are a bounded subgraph plus an optional cursor to resume. Cost is proportional to result, not graph size.

## D-029: Traversal is a pure function of (graph, spec) via a total tie-break cascade {.decision #d-029} ^d-029
date:: 2026-07-15
stage:: 6
status:: provisional
reversal:: A needed traversal semantics is inherently order-dependent in a way the cascade can't make total.

Wherever the graph offers a choice of next edge, break ties by: containment `order` → cross-ref (edge-type name → target canonical id → edge id) → property sort key with node-id tie-break → visit-once by node id. Total because ids are totally orderable (D-014). Traversal output is reproducible across conforming engines.

## D-030: Queries are self-hosted (a query/view is a node) {.decision #d-030} ^d-030
date:: 2026-07-15
stage:: 7
status:: provisional
reversal:: Self-hosting queries proves too clumsy vs. a dedicated query representation.

A query is a node of kind `query`/`view` whose properties specify the seven traversal axes (D-026) plus a projection. Saved views are first-class knowledge (addressable, versionable, composable). Query *syntax* is deferred to Phase D.

## D-031: Filter axis is a decidable, per-node-local boolean predicate algebra {.decision #d-031} ^d-031
date:: 2026-07-15
stage:: 7
status:: provisional
reversal:: A common, legitimate query provably can't be expressed and isn't reasonably the agent's job (RM16).

Atomic predicates: type-in, has-tag, prop compare (=,≠,<,≤,>,≥), prop exists/contains, status, asserted-by class, has-edge — combined by AND/OR/NOT. Excluded: arithmetic, user functions, recursion, arbitrary joins. Aggregation (count/group) is a separate post-query result transform. Test: every predicate answerable per-node-locally with no unbounded computation.

## D-032: A query returns a result subgraph carrying stable ids + projection {.decision #d-032} ^d-032
date:: 2026-07-15
stage:: 7
status:: provisional
reversal:: The subgraph result shape proves insufficient for a required read pattern.

Result = matched nodes+edges, each carrying its stable id and a caller-specified projection (default: id+type+name+snippet; expandable), in deterministic order (D-029), with an optional continuation cursor (D-028) and diagnostics. Retracted excluded unless queried; derived marked `inferred`.

## D-033: Query results are the sole addressing mechanism for operations (read/write bridge) {.decision #d-033} ^d-033
date:: 2026-07-15
stage:: 7
status:: provisional
reversal:: None foreseen; this is the linchpin of the AI-native efficiency claim.

Operations (Stage 8) target node/edge ids surfaced by query results. The agent loop is query→reason→operate(by id)→re-query. Positions are never an edit target.

## D-034: Composition = set-algebra + runtime construction over base queries {.decision #d-034} ^d-034
date:: 2026-07-15
stage:: 7
status:: provisional
reversal:: A needed composition can't be expressed as set-algebra over results.

Parallel = `union` of results (dedupe by id); comparative = `intersect`/`difference` + id/name alignment; AI-selected = the agent constructs a query node at runtime. The strategies are set-algebra and runtime construction over the base query (D-030), not new primitives.

## D-035: Two-layer operation set (8 primitives + composite macros + compact) {.decision #d-035} ^d-035
date:: 2026-07-15
stage:: 8
status:: provisional
reversal:: A required edit can't be expressed as a primitive/composite without breaking an invariant.

8 primitives — create-node, retract-node, set-content, set-property, unset-property, add-edge, retract-edge, move — complete and closed under the 10 invariants (Stage 4 §11). Containment is edited only via create-node/move (protects single-home); nothing destroys. Composites (merge, split, promote, demote) are atomic macros = primitive sequences. tag = add-edge; reorder = move. `compact` is the sole destructive op, explicit and separate.

## D-036: Ops address only by id; no positional addressing {.decision #d-036} ^d-036
date:: 2026-07-15
stage:: 8
status:: provisional
reversal:: None foreseen; positional addressing is incompatible with convergence.

Every op targets node/edge ids from query results; create-node mints a new collision-free id (D-014); no op references a line/offset/index.

## D-037: Convergence by design (LWW registers + grow-sets → SEC) {.decision #d-037} ^d-037
date:: 2026-07-15
stage:: 8
status:: provisional
reversal:: A required edit semantics cannot be made commutative/convergent.

create/add = grow-sets; retract = status flag (retract-wins); set-property/set-content/move = LWW-registers with Lamport-ts tie-break; list-valued props may opt into OR-Set semantics. The state-fold (partition by target+field; max-ts for LWW, union for sets) is order-independent → Strong Eventual Consistency; CRDT-ready without model change. v1 content merge is per-node LWW (coarse; RM18).

## D-038: Optimistic-concurrency preconditions (solves RM17) {.decision #d-038} ^d-038
date:: 2026-07-15
stage:: 8
status:: provisional
reversal:: Preconditions prove insufficient and a stronger transactional model is required.

An op may carry an `expect(target, version=v | field OP value)` precondition; if it fails the op is rejected and the caller re-queries. Default (unguarded) = LWW converge; guarded = check-and-set. The version seen at query becomes the precondition at write.

## D-039: Op-log is canonical; state = deterministic fold (event sourcing) {.decision #d-039} ^d-039
date:: 2026-07-15
stage:: 8
status:: provisional
reversal:: Fold cost at scale forces a materialized-state-as-truth model (op-log demoted to audit).

The append-only op-log is the journal; state = order-independent fold over the op-set (D-037). Complete-rebuild and temporal-query follow. Semantic op-log↔state equivalence established here; byte-level demo completed in Stage 9 (needs the canonical form). Underwrites the file-as-truth fallback (RM8): file = op-log + snapshot if a live store is ever needed.

## D-040: One model, three serializations {.decision #d-040} ^d-040
date:: 2026-07-15
stage:: 9
status:: provisional
reversal:: Maintaining three serializations proves to cause drift/inconsistency that a single form would avoid.

Three serializations of one model: (a) canonical normal form (hash/sign/dedup/diff), (b) append-only op-log (edits/sync/cache), (c) author-facing text (Phase D). All inter-convert losslessly; author text normalizes to the canonical form ("write loose, store canonical" at the byte level, D-003). JSON is the machine encoding for (a)/(b), never the author surface.

## D-041: Canonical normal form = line-oriented canonical JSON (RFC 8785) {.decision #d-041} ^d-041
date:: 2026-07-15
stage:: 9
status:: provisional
reversal:: JCS-style canonical JSON proves unable to encode a needed model element losslessly.

`canon: State→Bytes` — document-order nodes, deterministic edge/property ordering (D-029 cascade), canonical scalars, NFC strings, fixed field order; line-oriented so one semantic change = one small diff and `hash(canon)` is stable. Realized as canonical JSON (JCS/RFC 8785 rules) over the `.sarib`⇄JSON isomorphism — don't reinvent canonicalization.

## D-042: File = canonical snapshot + append-only op-log {.decision #d-042} ^d-042
date:: 2026-07-15
stage:: 9
status:: provisional
reversal:: Snapshot+log proves worse than a single materialized file for real workloads.

A stored file = optional canonical snapshot + append-only op-log suffix; read = load snapshot + fold suffix; canonical *state* is content-addressed/hashed, the log carries history/sync. Append-only growth keeps KV-cache prefixes stable. This IS the "demote to live store + journal" fallback, so RM8 needs no model change.

## D-043: Load safety — pure data, bounded expansion, canonicalization resistance {.decision #d-043} ^d-043
date:: 2026-07-15
stage:: 9
status:: provisional
reversal:: A required feature genuinely needs load-time evaluation (would demand a sandbox spec instead).

Pure-data load (no tags/constructors/macros/directives that execute); transclusion resolution is cycle-detected + depth/size-bounded; the canonicalizer rejects ambiguous encodings (duplicate keys, non-NFC, non-canonical numbers). Content is inert data, never instructions (format-level RS3 defense; the Crockford-removed-comments discipline).

## D-044: Partial/streaming load via addressable records + derived index {.decision #d-044} ^d-044
date:: 2026-07-15
stage:: 9
status:: provisional
reversal:: Addressable-record layout proves incompatible with a needed canonical-form property.

Records are id-addressable; a derived, disposable id→byte-offset index gives random access; containment-order sections are contiguous byte ranges; locality (P15) guarantees streaming and bounded-subgraph loads (D-028). The index is derived-layer (P17), never canonical.

## D-045: Author surface = CommonMark superset (Candidate A recommended; B retained) {.decision #d-045} ^d-045
date:: 2026-07-15
stage:: 10
status:: provisional
reversal:: Writability testing shows authors prefer B's density, or A's Markdown constraints block a needed construct.

The surface is a CommonMark superset taking djot's discipline (unambiguous glyphs, attributes-on-any-element, no-backtracking locality) but a Pandoc/MyST/Dataview-compatible surface that degrades to literal text in vanilla renderers. **Candidate A (prose-native) is the recommended default**; Candidate B (outline-dense) is retained as an alternative and future compact profile. Both ship as judgeable example packages and normalize to the same model/canonical form.

## D-046: Surface conventions (containment/type/props/edges/id/meta) {.decision #d-046} ^d-046
date:: 2026-07-15
stage:: 10
status:: provisional
reversal:: A convention proves to fragment tokens or collide ambiguously (RA11).

headings + list nesting → containment; trailing `{.type #slug}` → node type/slug; `key:: value` inline fields → properties; `[rel:: [[Target]]]` → typed edges (untyped `[[Target]]` → `relates-to`); `^id` → block identity; YAML front matter → file metadata. Glyphs drawn from the single-token ASCII set; multi-char sigils measured against real tokenizers before freeze.

## D-047: Spatial legibility via derived, optional annotations {.decision #d-047} ^d-047
date:: 2026-07-15
stage:: 10
status:: provisional
reversal:: Derived cues prove insufficient and authors need to hand-place shape hints.

Deliver shape via **derived, optional** cues — statistics-cookie counts `[k/n]`, dotted-path/breadcrumb depth, ordinal position, fold/`…` markers, a generated typed skeleton/TOC, container summaries — regenerated from the model, never authored, never canonical (P17/D-019). Stable ids double as spatial anchors.

## D-048: Importance is a field, not typography; ship two judgeable syntaxes {.decision #d-048} ^d-048
date:: 2026-07-15
stage:: 10
status:: provisional
reversal:: A field-based importance proves less usable than a typographic convention in testing.

Priority/weight/importance is an addressable field (`priority::`), queryable and projection-stable; typographic emphasis is for human scanning only. Two full surfaces (A, B) are shipped as independently-judgeable example packages per Sarib's steer on taste-dependent choices.

## D-049: Three validation tiers; only un-parseability blocks {.decision #d-049} ^d-049
date:: 2026-07-15
stage:: 11
status:: provisional
reversal:: A use case requires hard-blocking on schema violations (would add an opt-in strict mode, not change the default).

Tier 0 well-formed (total; unrecognized input → L0 prose node; near-unfailable), Tier 1 structurally valid (the 10 invariants), Tier 2 schema-valid (active vocabulary). Nothing above Tier 0 is fatal; all deviations are located, non-fatal diagnostics carrying node/edge ids.

## D-050: Self-hosted, closed-world, deterministic validation {.decision #d-050} ^d-050
date:: 2026-07-15
stage:: 11
status:: provisional
reversal:: Self-hosted schemas prove unable to express a needed constraint class.

Schemas are `.sarib` checked by a meta-schema; no second validation language; validation is closed-world (unknown-vs-active-schema = diagnostic, no inference); diagnostics are deterministic, canonical-ordered, and queryable (self-hosted as derived nodes).

## D-051: Fidelity contract — idempotent normalization, lossless round-trip, read-transparent cues {.decision #d-051} ^d-051
date:: 2026-07-15
stage:: 11
status:: provisional
reversal:: Idempotent normalization proves impossible for a needed construct.

`normalize(parse(surface))` = canonical form and is idempotent (a gofmt for `.sarib`); model-level round-trip is lossless (incidental formatting may change, knowledge never does); derived cues are ignored on parse and regenerated on render, so staleness/hand-edits are never errors.

## D-052: Projection = query + template; all views (incl. the AI context window) are (query, template) pairs {.decision #d-052} ^d-052
date:: 2026-07-15
stage:: 12
status:: provisional
reversal:: A required view can't be expressed as (query, template) over the model.

A view = a query (subgraph + order, Stage 7) + a template (element→presentation), every projected element carrying its node/edge id. All brief views — document, outline, mind-map, dependency graph, board, timeline, table, slides, **AI context window** — are (query, template) pairs over the one model; no per-view engine. The agent's context window is a projection like any other (rendering-for-humans and rendering-for-agents are one operation).

## D-053: Every projection declares live-window vs terminal-export {.decision #d-053} ^d-053
date:: 2026-07-15
stage:: 12
status:: provisional
reversal:: None foreseen; this is the empirically decisive round-trip rule.

A projection is either a **live window** (edits become id-addressed operations, D-033) or a **terminal export** (read-only, self-declared, re-export to change). The ambiguous-editable-but-no-back-channel middle is forbidden (P17). Lossy live views hide but never drop fields.

## D-054: Derived spatial cues are computed per view on render {.decision #d-054} ^d-054
date:: 2026-07-15
stage:: 12
status:: provisional
reversal:: Per-view derived computation proves too costly and cues must be materialized (would carry `inferred` provenance, D-019).

Rendering computes skeleton/TOC, `[k/n]` counts, subtree size, ordinal position, fold markers, and container summaries from the model on demand, presented per view (board=column counts, timeline=span, outline=depth+child counts, document=TOC). Always regenerated, never authored/canonical (P17/D-051); ids double as spatial anchors.

## D-055: Reference architecture = 6 components as executable stages {.decision #d-055} ^d-055
date:: 2026-07-15
stage:: 13
status:: provisional
reversal:: A needed capability doesn't fit the component decomposition.

parser · normalizer · model store · op engine (with validation) · query engine · projector. Query+projector are one mechanism (a view = query+template, D-052); op engine + validator share invariant checks (RM14). Each component is the executable form of one stage; data flows in the read→edit→render loop, not a pipeline.

## D-056: Business-card parser — weekend / ≤~1000 LOC (S6) {.decision #d-056} ^d-056
date:: 2026-07-15
stage:: 13
status:: provisional
reversal:: Conformance genuinely requires more than ~1000 LOC (would signal the core grew too big — revisit priority rule 4).

A conforming Tier-0/1 parser is a weekend / ≤~1000 LOC build, made reachable by total+local+no-backtracking parsing (D-045/D-049), a business-card grammar (P16/D-018), and canonical-JSON reuse (D-041). Reference parsers ship in TypeScript/Python/Rust as adoption instruments (a free parser everywhere).

## D-057: Ship a consumer with v0.1 (MCP server + CLI) + harness + corpus {.decision #d-057} ^d-057
date:: 2026-07-15
stage:: 13
status:: provisional
reversal:: None foreseen; shipping a consumer is the adoption precondition.

The reference implementation ships a consumer with v0.1 — an MCP server (files as resources, ops as tools; the agent loop) and a `sarib` CLI (parse/fmt/query/apply/render/validate/diff), both thin transports over the components (D-035). A benchmark harness (S2/S4/S3/S6/RA11) and a conformance corpus (RG2) are required before spec freeze (Stage 15 gate).

## D-058: File conventions {.decision #d-058} ^d-058
date:: 2026-07-15
stage:: 14
status:: provisional
reversal:: Registration or ecosystem constraints require different conventions.

Extension `.sarib`; media type `text/sarib` (provisional registration target); UTF-8 + NFC; the file declares its core `sarib` version and pinned `vocab@version` in front matter.

## D-059: Compatibility contract {.decision #d-059} ^d-059
date:: 2026-07-15
stage:: 14
status:: provisional
reversal:: A required correction can't be expressed additively or as a clean major bump.

Frozen core (a document's meaning never changes under a later core revision); vocabularies semver, additive-only within a major; unknown core-minor/vocabulary degrades gracefully (unknown types→generic nodes, unknown props round-trip untouched), never fails, never silently reinterprets; deprecate-not-delete.

## D-060: v1.0 is a conditional proposal, gated on measured evidence {.decision #d-060} ^d-060
date:: 2026-07-15
stage:: 15
status:: provisional
reversal:: N/A — this is the project's terminal honesty condition; it can only be discharged by running the gate.

v1.0 is a *conditional* proposal — the specification is complete and internally consistent, but ratification/freeze is gated on the reference implementation clearing the Stage 15 §4 benchmark gate (success criteria S1–S8) and tokenizer-verifying the grammar (RA11). The standard ships only if measured evidence shows it beats the Markdown baseline (Rule 6). Overclaiming completion before this gate is drift.

## D-061: Candidate A ratified as the normative author surface (user judgment) {.decision #d-061} ^d-061
date:: 2026-07-19
stage:: post-15 execution (Sprint 0→1)
status:: ratified
reversal:: Freeze-gate benchmarks (G1–G8) reveal an A-specific failure that B avoids.

**Candidate A (prose-native Markdown superset) is the normative surface.** Candidate B is preserved as the future *compact profile* for token-critical agent↔agent exchange (not author-facing). Reference implementation (Python), conformance corpus, and benchmarks build against A.
